From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:21:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: dw-hdmi: Follow the TCON clock and redo the engine
 mode on format changes

Changing only the "max bpc" property (10-bit RGB to 8-bit RGB at the
same mode) sets connectors_changed, not mode_changed. The atomic helpers
then run the encoder mode set but skip mode_set_nofb(), so the display
engine formatter and the TCON stay on the previous output format while
dw-hdmi switches to the new one. Force mode_changed when the negotiated
format or YCbCr encoding changes.

The HDMI module clock was set to the TMDS rate, 5/4 of the pixel clock
for 10-bit. That rate is not reachable from the video PLL that clocks
the TCON (1080p60 10-bit got 169.7 MHz instead of 185.6 MHz). The
vendor driver sets this clock to the TCON TV clock rate for every
colour depth, and the Synopsys PHY PLL applies the deep colour factor
from its MPLL table. Do the same: the pixel clock, halved for YUV 4:2:0.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_dw_hdmi.c | 29 ++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_dw_hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_dw_hdmi.c
index 1bbd63e7c..a826ade4d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_dw_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_dw_hdmi.c
@@ -87,9 +87,16 @@ static int sun8i_hdmi_enc_atomic_check(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	old_scrtc_state = drm_crtc_state_to_sun4i_crtc_state(
 		drm_atomic_get_old_crtc_state(crtc_state->state, crtc_state->crtc));
 	if (scrtc_state->format != old_scrtc_state->format ||
-	    scrtc_state->encoding != old_scrtc_state->encoding)
+	    scrtc_state->encoding != old_scrtc_state->encoding) {
+		/*
+		 * A max bpc change alone only sets connectors_changed, which
+		 * skips mode_set_nofb(), where the engine and TCON take the
+		 * new format.
+		 */
+		crtc_state->mode_changed = true;
 		return drm_atomic_add_affected_planes(crtc_state->state,
 						      crtc_state->crtc);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -141,22 +148,16 @@ sun8i_dw_hdmi_encoder_atomic_mode_set(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 	unsigned long rate = mode->crtc_clock * 1000UL;
 
 	/*
-	 * The TMDS character rate is derived from the pixel clock: deep
-	 * color multiplies it (10-bit: 5/4), except for YUV 4:2:2, which
-	 * always uses 12-bit containers at the pixel rate, and YUV 4:2:0
-	 * halves it again since two horizontal samples share one TMDS
-	 * period.
+	 * This clock feeds the controller with the TCON output, like the
+	 * vendor driver, which sets it to the TCON TV clock rate: the pixel
+	 * clock, halved for YUV 4:2:0 as the TCON halves it. Deep colour
+	 * does not change it (the PHY PLL multiplies the TMDS rate), and a
+	 * 5/4 rate is not reachable from the video PLL that clocks the TCON.
 	 */
 	switch (scrtc_state->link_format) {
-	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RGB101010_1X30:
-	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_YUV10_1X30:
-		rate = rate * 5 / 4;
-		break;
-	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_UYYVYY10_0_5X30:
-		rate = rate * 5 / 4 / 2;
-		break;
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_UYYVYY8_0_5X24:
-		rate = rate / 2;
+	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_UYYVYY10_0_5X30:
+		rate /= 2;
 		break;
 	default:
 		break;
-- 
